From 8b6fdd666c43fe0810eb8f6f321981a0c2a86d62 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Noel Blatter <noel.blatter@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 23:52:56 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Docker image with bytecode, like a checkout with pip install

The Dockerfile set PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 before pip ran. pip then installs
every package without .pyc files, and each run in the container compiles JAX,
NumPy and all other modules again, inside the timed import phase. In addition
.dockerignore left out every __pycache__, so the shipped, hash-checked
bytecode of differometor was missing in the image as well.

Same code (9a31fa1), 6 alternating runs on an M4 with one CPU: imports
248.3 -> 113.2 ms, complete first run 320.0 -> 187.0 ms. Nothing changes for
a run outside Docker.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .dockerignore | 1 -
 Dockerfile    | 6 +++++-
 2 files changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/.dockerignore b/.dockerignore
index 8f3fd1f..00cc293 100644
--- a/.dockerignore
+++ b/.dockerignore
@@ -1,6 +1,5 @@
 .git
 .venv
-**/__pycache__
 *.egg-info
 runs/*.npz
 runs/*.log
diff --git a/Dockerfile b/Dockerfile
index 19d11b9..2146258 100644
--- a/Dockerfile
+++ b/Dockerfile
@@ -1,7 +1,11 @@
 # Linux environment for `python benchmark.py --cpus 1` (CPU affinity needs Linux).
 FROM python:3.12-slim
 
-ENV PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 PIP_NO_CACHE_DIR=1 PIP_DISABLE_PIP_VERSION_CHECK=1
+# PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE is deliberately not set: with it pip installs every package without
+# bytecode, and each run in the container compiles JAX, NumPy and everything else again inside
+# the timed import phase (imports 258 ms instead of 116 ms on an M4). The image is meant to behave
+# like a checkout with `pip install`, which is what the benchmark is measured in.
+ENV PIP_NO_CACHE_DIR=1 PIP_DISABLE_PIP_VERSION_CHECK=1
 WORKDIR /app
 
 # Dependencies first so code changes do not invalidate this layer.
-- 
